What is the Tries:
   It is a data structure used in Dictionary, to store less number of words (ex:1000), We can use HashMap but if we want to store millions
   of words then we have to go with tries because there is a memory constraints.
   
   In Tries data structure if we have common characters between the words then they share the common memory. Example (do, done, dont)
   Here d & o stored in a memory and shared across all three examples.
   
 Tries Implementation:
     To implement TrieNode, we required three variables 1) To store the data of char type 2) To check whether the node isTerminal
     3) Each node will have a Trie Node Array of size 26, by default all the node values are null.
     
HashMap vs Tries:
   1) When comes to time complexity both of them are same, but when comes to space HashMap consumes more space compared to trie because 
for each word in HashMap, different memory will be allocated but in case of trie memory will be shared across the words.

